    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d721">

                <pb facs="0704" n="588" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg588"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 294.11Ei5/7.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Ambassador
                    Guthrie</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-10-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 17, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your telegram of October 15. Formal extradition papers, which have been passed
                    upon by this Department and found to be in proper <pb facs="0705" n="589"
                        xml:id="pg589"/> form, have been forwarded to you. You will see that every
                    precaution is taken to prevent injury to child by Eills, and you are not
                    authorized to consent to his release on bail.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moore.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
